<title>INDIA: India produces 4,190 T copper cathodes in November.</title>
<headline>India produces 4,190 T copper cathodes in November.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-12-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's state-run Hindustan Copper Ltd (HCL) produced 4,190 tonnes of copper cathodes in November against a target of 4,340 tonnes, a government statement said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>It produced 3,075 tonnes of continous cast copper rods against a target of 3,500 tonnes, the statement said.</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>	    Installed     November 96	   Cumulative output</p>
<p>	    capacity   --------------------- ---------------------</p>
<p>	    (annual)   Target	 Actual   Apr-Nov 96 Apr-Nov 95</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Copper</p>
<p> cathodes   47,500   4,340	  4,190	22,467	25,242</p>
<p>Copper</p>
<p> rods	 60,000   3,500	  3,075	26,080	21,278</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>NOTE: Figures in tonnes and provisional.</p>
</text>
